    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93-a1">

                <pb facs="0212" n="124" xml:id="pg124"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 736.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Leonard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 64.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of yonr
                    dispatch No. 198 of May 31 last, in relation to the question of jurisdiction in
                    the case of James A. Frame, charged with killing George Lemon, and to say that
                    the Department considers it quite clear that you should try this ease in the
                    manner provided by law.</p>
                <p>I may add that a jailer or marshal is not considered a consular officer within
                    the intendment of the statute.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Second Assistant Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
